+// ebony-joins.md 7.1 X4-a to X4-f). Blocks, each after the app's r16 gate; no model; x3's loader, kernels, rings and arms reused:
+//   x4i  CL_DEVICE_EXTENSIONS in full, SVM capabilities, CL_DEVICE_RECORDABLE_QUEUE_MAX_SIZE (qcom), entry points; compiles
+//        the four upstream kernels in the clc child (x3b's path; later blocks load the binaries)
+//   x4a  launch timeline on the profiling queue: 8 launches of 2816x4096 then one clFinish; one Llama-2 layer (7 launches);
+//        the 8 with clFlush after each; QUEUED / SUBMIT / START / END of every event; launcher on 0-3 (as R74) and on cpu 4
+//   x4b  the x3 rt cell at 2816 rows from 0-3, cpu 4, cpu 7 (each after a 0.5 s spin to full clock) x wait by clFinish,
+//        clFlush + event status spin, clFlush + clWaitForEvents
+//   x4f  launch-ahead behind a user event set about 1 ms later; rt with SetKernelArg cut to the 2 args that change
+//   x4c  stacked buffers gate||up 22016x4096 and q||k||v 12288x4096 on the general kernel: identity and cold rate
+//   x4d  recordable queue (cl_qcom_recordable_queues): record a Llama-2 layer, replay, against sync1 (child process)
+//   x4e  persistent kernel: CPU -> running kernel flag, kernel -> CPU counter, looped row-claiming gemv (child processes)
+//   x4m  upstream's multi-column gemv (_mc3) at n_cols 2, 3, 4 on 11008x4096: identity per column, cold dev time against 1 column
+//   x4s  row split of a fused [gate;up] at batch 1, GPU share 0.20 to 0.60: launch from the pool's lead thread on cpu 4,
+//        clFlush, CPU rows, event spin; the R74 feeder mode at 0.25 as anchor
+//   x4r  residency with 1.5 GB of GPU buffers beside a 2.6 GB anonymous arena
+// The child blocks (x4d_c, x4e1_c, x4e2_c, x4e3_c) run in libvollie_x4c.so (tools/c3_x4child.c: loads libllama.so, calls this
+// entry with VOLLIE_PROBE_TEE=1 so each line is written to stdout at once), killed at a timeout; the parent copies the x4 lines.
+namespace r35 {
+using namespace r34;
